WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.320
Every trade in a free market is voluntary.

2
00:00:03.320 --> 00:00:06.320
The buyer pays less than
the good is worth to them.

3
00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:09.660
The seller gets more than
the least they would accept.

4
00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:11.910
Both walk away better off.

5
00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:13.870
Add up millions of these trades,

6
00:00:13.870 --> 00:00:16.680
and surely the market
makes the right amount.

7
00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:18.650
Yet often it makes too much,

8
00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:20.120
or too little.

9
00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:22.830
So if buyers and sellers both gain,

10
00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:26.360
how can a free market still
produce the wrong amount?

11
00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:29.070
In this mission, you'll
find the point where society

12
00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:31.130
gains the most from a market.

13
00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:33.820
Then you'll move output
away from that point,

14
00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:35.970
and see what happens to the gain.

15
00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:39.810
Your mission: find out when a
market's answer is the wrong one.
